    <decisions>
        <description>recipientUserIds is a semicolon-delimited string of selected User Ids (this is what a Multi-Select Checkboxes screen field naturally outputs, so callers never need to build a real collection). Contains is a substring check, so this only matches on the full Id.</description>
        <name>Is_Selected_Recipient</name>
        <label>Is Selected Recipient?</label>
        <locationX>0</locationX>
        <locationY>0</locationY>
        <defaultConnector>
            <targetReference>Loop_Recipient_Users</targetReference>
        </defaultConnector>
        <defaultConnectorLabel>Not Selected</defaultConnectorLabel>
        <rules>
            <name>Selected</name>
            <conditionLogic>and</conditionLogic>
            <conditions>
                <leftValueReference>recipientUserIds</leftValueReference>
                <operator>Contains</operator>
                <rightValue>
                    <elementReference>Loop_Recipient_Users.Id</elementReference>
                </rightValue>
            </conditions>
            <connector>
                <targetReference>Add_Email_To_List</targetReference>
            </connector>
            <label>Selected</label>
        </rules>
    </decisions>
    <description>Shared, content-agnostic notification sender. Callers (DWDECI-39 &quot;Notify Team&quot; from Interaction, and DWDECI-41 &quot;Notify Staff&quot; from Record Alert) compose their own subject/body/record link and pass recipientUserIds as a semicolon-delimited string of User Ids (the natural output shape of a Multi-Select Checkboxes screen field, so callers never need to build a real collection); this subflow matches against all active users and sends the email. Fault path -&gt; ErrorLogger.logFromFlow (ACC Base Utilities Log Error action).</description>
